1
00:02:30,142 --> 00:02:35,142
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,142 --> 00:02:39,142
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:39,142 --> 00:02:44,142
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,142 --> 00:02:48,142
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:48,142 --> 00:02:51,142
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:51,142 --> 00:02:54,142
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:54,142 --> 00:02:57,142
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:57,142 --> 00:03:00,142
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:02,142 --> 00:03:04,142
Now this is exciting!

10
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:07,142
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:07,142 --> 00:03:10,142
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:10,142 --> 00:03:15,142
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:19,142 --> 00:03:21,142
Separated from the rest of his crew,

14
00:03:21,142 --> 00:03:24,142
Luffy launched a desperate attack on Navy Headquarters

15
00:03:24,142 --> 00:03:27,142
in hopes of saving his brother from execution.

16
00:03:27,142 --> 00:03:30,142
However, his struggle ended in vain,

17
00:03:30,142 --> 00:03:33,142
with his enemies claiming an overwhelming victory,

18
00:03:33,142 --> 00:03:35,142
along with Ace's life.

19
00:03:39,142 --> 00:03:42,142
But Brother Ace is really dead, isn't he?

20
00:03:43,142 --> 00:03:45,142
Yes, I'm afraid that he is.

21
00:03:45,142 --> 00:04:10,142
Luffy and Ace, the story of how the brothers met.

22
00:04:10,142 --> 00:04:20,142
No one could have guessed it at the time,

23
00:04:20,142 --> 00:04:24,142
but the path that led Luffy to Marineford began long ago.

24
00:04:24,142 --> 00:04:27,142
Ten years ago, in fact, in the East Blue.

25
00:04:30,142 --> 00:04:33,142
There lies a small town known as Windmill Village,

26
00:04:33,142 --> 00:04:36,142
where people lived quiet, peaceful lives.

27
00:04:36,142 --> 00:04:38,142
But it was the nearby Mount Corvo,

28
00:04:38,142 --> 00:04:41,142
where few would dare to set foot.

29
00:04:41,142 --> 00:04:44,142
For only the strong could survive in its dark woods,

30
00:04:44,142 --> 00:04:48,142
faced with beasts that would make quick work of trespassers.

31
00:04:49,142 --> 00:04:52,142
What's wrong with being king of the pirates, Grandpa?

32
00:04:53,142 --> 00:04:56,142
The pirates are... cool!

33
00:04:56,142 --> 00:04:58,142
And what makes you think I care?

34
00:04:58,142 --> 00:05:00,142
I'm gonna... slap you!

35
00:05:00,142 --> 00:05:03,142
Eating that devil fruit wasn't enough trouble for you?

36
00:05:03,142 --> 00:05:04,142
Now this nonsense?

37
00:05:04,142 --> 00:05:06,142
You and your big brother, Ace,

38
00:05:06,142 --> 00:05:08,142
are going to become fine Marines.

39
00:05:08,142 --> 00:05:09,142
You understand me?

40
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:11,142
Ow, ow, ow, you suck!

41
00:05:11,142 --> 00:05:13,142
I thought I was supposed to be made out of rubber now.

42
00:05:13,142 --> 00:05:15,142
Why does this still hurt so much?

43
00:05:16,142 --> 00:05:19,142
I thought leaving you in a nice village would keep you safe,

44
00:05:19,142 --> 00:05:21,142
but pirates won't be satisfied

45
00:05:21,142 --> 00:05:23,142
until they get their grubby hands on everything.

46
00:05:23,142 --> 00:05:26,142
And I forbid you to associate with that red-haired Shanks.

47
00:05:26,142 --> 00:05:28,142
He's a terrible influence.

48
00:05:28,142 --> 00:05:30,142
Ah, it's awesome!

49
00:05:30,142 --> 00:05:32,142
Now I'm gonna be just like it!

50
00:05:32,142 --> 00:05:33,142
Oh, yeah!

51
00:05:42,142 --> 00:05:43,142
What's this dump?

52
00:05:46,142 --> 00:05:47,142
Hey, shut the hell up!

53
00:05:48,142 --> 00:05:50,142
Whatever it is you're selling, I don't want knives!

54
00:05:50,142 --> 00:05:51,142
Put it on!

55
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:52,142
Huh?

56
00:05:52,142 --> 00:05:53,142
Huh?

57
00:05:53,142 --> 00:05:54,142
Ah!

58
00:05:54,142 --> 00:05:56,142
Garp, what are you doing here?

59
00:05:56,142 --> 00:05:57,142
Hmmm...

60
00:06:10,142 --> 00:06:11,142
Charming as ever.

61
00:06:11,142 --> 00:06:13,142
Sorry for the cold welcome,

62
00:06:13,142 --> 00:06:16,142
but I hope you don't have another ridiculous favor to ask us.

63
00:06:16,142 --> 00:06:18,622
You realize Ace is already ten, right?

64
00:06:19,082 --> 00:06:20,022
Oh, is he now?

65
00:06:20,162 --> 00:06:22,002
And how's the little scam doing? Good?

66
00:06:22,282 --> 00:06:24,342
Well, there's a handful, of course.

67
00:06:24,482 --> 00:06:26,902
And we've been watching over the brat for long enough.

68
00:06:26,982 --> 00:06:28,242
So just take him away.

69
00:06:28,342 --> 00:06:28,802
Never mind.

70
00:06:29,362 --> 00:06:31,522
Yeah, that's the problem. We do mind.

71
00:06:31,622 --> 00:06:33,682
Speaking of breath, would you shut that one up?

72
00:06:33,902 --> 00:06:35,042
He's yours now.

73
00:06:37,042 --> 00:06:39,002
Hey, Luffy, tell him hello.

74
00:06:39,342 --> 00:06:39,742
Yo!

75
00:06:40,042 --> 00:06:42,502
Wait a sec. Who is he?

76
00:06:42,802 --> 00:06:44,582
He's my grandson.

77
00:06:45,242 --> 00:06:45,762
Huh?

78
00:06:46,142 --> 00:06:46,942
What?

79
00:06:48,462 --> 00:06:50,022
I never heard about this.

80
00:06:50,122 --> 00:06:52,362
And you want us to take care of the little monster.

81
00:06:52,502 --> 00:06:54,002
A little darling, I mean.

82
00:06:54,562 --> 00:06:55,622
Well, no way.

83
00:06:55,842 --> 00:06:57,642
Fine. Then I'll give you two choices.

84
00:06:58,202 --> 00:07:01,282
You can either raise my grandson or spend your life in prison.

85
00:07:01,722 --> 00:07:04,042
Pretty generous, considering all the crimes you've committed.

86
00:07:06,622 --> 00:07:07,782
No fair.

87
00:07:08,622 --> 00:07:11,402
The thing is, I'd rather stay out of the slammer.

88
00:07:11,402 --> 00:07:14,522
Frankly, if you ask me that on one of Ace's bad days,

89
00:07:14,522 --> 00:07:17,082
I might have to go for the prison option after all.

90
00:07:17,142 --> 00:07:18,062
And two brats?

91
00:07:18,202 --> 00:07:19,382
Yeah, I don't think so.

92
00:07:19,782 --> 00:07:21,902
This kid looks like a real charmer, too.

93
00:07:22,382 --> 00:07:23,642
Like your face?

94
00:07:23,862 --> 00:07:25,502
You want to fight, you little punk?

95
00:07:25,502 --> 00:07:26,282
He, he, he, he, he.

96
00:07:26,282 --> 00:07:26,602
Oh!

97
00:07:27,102 --> 00:07:27,622
The door!

98
00:07:27,622 --> 00:07:27,702
The door!

99
00:07:28,122 --> 00:07:29,582
Don't let him get to you!

100
00:07:29,622 --> 00:07:29,882
Huh?

101
00:07:30,522 --> 00:07:31,082
Ew!

102
00:07:31,302 --> 00:07:31,782
Spit!

103
00:07:32,002 --> 00:07:32,862
That's gross!

104
00:07:33,442 --> 00:07:34,442
Who did that?

105
00:07:35,722 --> 00:07:36,322
Hey!

106
00:07:36,642 --> 00:07:37,382
You jerk!

107
00:07:37,802 --> 00:07:39,682
You better apologize for that!

108
00:07:39,682 --> 00:07:39,962
Huh?

109
00:07:40,322 --> 00:07:40,802
Hey!

110
00:07:41,022 --> 00:07:41,682
There he is!

111
00:07:42,062 --> 00:07:43,342
Oh, hello, Ace!

112
00:07:43,382 --> 00:07:44,342
Welcome back!

113
00:07:50,142 --> 00:07:51,242
I'm waiting!

114
00:07:53,962 --> 00:07:55,622
Luffy, this here is Ace.

115
00:07:56,082 --> 00:07:57,842
He's three years older than you.

116
00:07:58,102 --> 00:08:01,302
Anyway, you're going to be living with him and Dadan from now on.

117
00:08:01,722 --> 00:08:02,082
What?

118
00:08:02,542 --> 00:08:03,662
Not so fast!

119
00:08:03,662 --> 00:08:10,442
You play nice.

120
00:08:10,582 --> 00:08:11,602
We said no!

121
00:08:12,322 --> 00:08:13,502
You'll do it.

122
00:08:15,922 --> 00:08:17,462
Sir, as you wish, sir!

123
00:08:17,902 --> 00:08:19,542
Well, time to hit the road.

124
00:08:20,022 --> 00:08:22,002
I'll stop by again when I have time.

125
00:08:22,122 --> 00:08:23,722
What about some child support?

126
00:08:23,922 --> 00:08:25,002
Put it on my tab.

127
00:08:25,162 --> 00:08:26,182
This isn't a bar.

128
00:08:26,622 --> 00:08:26,922
Huh?

129
00:08:27,122 --> 00:08:27,482
Nothing!

130
00:08:27,622 --> 00:08:28,262
Come back soon!

131
00:08:28,622 --> 00:08:29,782
Boss, we're bandits.

132
00:08:29,922 --> 00:08:31,482
We can't take in another kid.

133
00:08:31,662 --> 00:08:32,742
Shut up and fix dinner.

134
00:08:32,742 --> 00:08:33,762
We'll figure it out.

135
00:08:33,862 --> 00:08:34,502
Thanks, ma'am.

136
00:08:35,402 --> 00:08:36,502
Say you're sorry!

137
00:08:36,962 --> 00:08:37,862
Hey, come back!

138
00:08:39,902 --> 00:08:41,742
I'll leave this hat to you.

139
00:08:54,982 --> 00:08:56,342
Where did he go?

140
00:08:58,322 --> 00:08:58,962
Hold it!

141
00:08:59,522 --> 00:09:00,482
Let me go!

142
00:09:00,562 --> 00:09:02,622
Give me all your money or I'll kill you!

143
00:09:02,742 --> 00:09:03,862
I don't got any.

144
00:09:03,962 --> 00:09:04,542
I'm a kid!

145
00:09:04,622 --> 00:09:05,002
Fine!

146
00:09:05,182 --> 00:09:07,462
Then go tell your parents to bring us their money!

147
00:09:07,622 --> 00:09:08,362
I have a grandpa!

148
00:09:08,582 --> 00:09:09,562
Okay, good enough.

149
00:09:09,702 --> 00:09:11,562
Tell us his name and we'll go find him.

150
00:09:11,802 --> 00:09:12,622
It's Garp.

151
00:09:13,842 --> 00:09:15,142
Not the Garp!

152
00:09:15,302 --> 00:09:18,002
And the kid's going to be staying with us from now on.

153
00:09:18,342 --> 00:09:20,062
How did you agree to this?

154
00:09:20,182 --> 00:09:22,222
We're not running a daycare here!

155
00:09:22,582 --> 00:09:23,802
Screw a spine!

156
00:09:23,802 --> 00:09:24,922
That's enough!

157
00:09:24,922 --> 00:09:27,302
It's dinner time, boys!

158
00:09:27,422 --> 00:09:28,882
You can argue when you die!

159
00:09:31,102 --> 00:09:32,542
I want the big one!

160
00:09:32,542 --> 00:09:33,042
Screw you!

161
00:09:33,142 --> 00:09:34,122
Lights on first!

162
00:09:34,262 --> 00:09:35,522
See some for me!

163
00:09:36,642 --> 00:09:37,162
Hey!

164
00:09:37,662 --> 00:09:39,442
You already ate your affair, pal!

165
00:09:39,482 --> 00:09:39,922
Give me!

166
00:09:40,342 --> 00:09:42,202
I'm not losing to you, youngster!

167
00:09:42,542 --> 00:09:43,742
You share or you die!

168
00:09:43,882 --> 00:09:45,602
Survival of the fittest, my friends.

169
00:09:45,602 --> 00:09:49,082
Broke his arm!

170
00:09:52,202 --> 00:09:53,362
Come on!

171
00:09:55,762 --> 00:09:56,942
It's your turn to do this.

172
00:09:57,862 --> 00:09:58,822
Oh, man.

173
00:09:58,982 --> 00:10:00,042
Can I have some more?

174
00:10:00,142 --> 00:10:02,502
I'm a woman, thank you very much!

175
00:10:02,782 --> 00:10:05,522
Do you even know where you are right now, you filthy little urchin?

176
00:10:05,802 --> 00:10:06,182
No.

177
00:10:06,442 --> 00:10:07,722
Okay, then I'll tell you.

178
00:10:08,002 --> 00:10:09,762
This is the den of the Dodon family.

179
00:10:09,922 --> 00:10:11,922
Mountain bandits that rule Mount Corvo.

180
00:10:11,982 --> 00:10:12,702
Mountain bandits?

181
00:10:12,702 --> 00:10:15,862
Mountain bandits are lame.

182
00:10:17,042 --> 00:10:18,602
Well, you're stuck with us.

183
00:10:18,782 --> 00:10:22,262
Or rather, we're stuck with you, thanks to that pushy grandfather of yours.

184
00:10:22,362 --> 00:10:24,422
But if you don't want to stay, that's fine by me.

185
00:10:24,522 --> 00:10:26,622
Go get eaten by a bunch of wolves for all I care.

186
00:10:26,682 --> 00:10:28,202
Easy, boss. Easy.

187
00:10:28,662 --> 00:10:30,442
I just wanted some more rice.

188
00:10:32,122 --> 00:10:34,202
For me, it would be nice.

189
00:10:34,202 --> 00:10:45,762
In case you didn't notice, all this meat came from that bison ace brought back.

190
00:10:45,882 --> 00:10:49,002
Even though he's a kid like you, he has to work to earn his cape.

191
00:10:49,162 --> 00:10:51,022
The bandits' life's a hardwood boy.

192
00:10:51,022 --> 00:10:54,122
Tomorrow, you're going to pay in blood, sweat, and tears.

193
00:10:54,682 --> 00:10:55,242
Cleaning.

194
00:10:55,482 --> 00:10:56,342
Doing laundry.

195
00:10:56,762 --> 00:10:58,382
Policing our boots and weapons.

196
00:10:58,782 --> 00:11:00,562
Robbery, fraud, murder, and terror.

197
00:11:01,482 --> 00:11:06,562
And if you go crying to your dear old grandpa, we'll string you up without a second thought.

198
00:11:06,942 --> 00:11:10,842
One bowl of rice and one glass of water, that's all I can promise you.

199
00:11:11,302 --> 00:11:12,642
The rest you get for yourself.

200
00:11:13,562 --> 00:11:15,982
You're going to have to grow up real fast, kid.

201
00:11:16,122 --> 00:11:18,122
Or you're going to go hungry before the week's up.

202
00:11:18,142 --> 00:11:18,702
No problem.

203
00:11:18,962 --> 00:11:19,742
No problem?

204
00:11:20,202 --> 00:11:22,202
Not crying and begging for mercy?

205
00:11:22,362 --> 00:11:26,082
Grandpa threw me in the jungle one time, so I know how to tough it out just fine.

206
00:11:26,242 --> 00:11:30,502
There's plenty of water to drink, and I can eat frogs and snakes and mushrooms and stuff all I want.

207
00:11:31,462 --> 00:11:34,322
I'm going to be a pirate someday, so we've got to be strong.

208
00:11:34,882 --> 00:11:36,622
This is going to be real fun.

209
00:11:37,802 --> 00:11:38,202
Boss!

210
00:11:38,402 --> 00:11:38,982
You okay?

211
00:11:39,342 --> 00:11:40,422
Hurry, help her up!

212
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:42,402
Keep home!

213
00:11:42,642 --> 00:11:45,962
Why is he leaving?

214
00:11:45,962 --> 00:11:47,342
One more!

215
00:11:48,662 --> 00:11:50,282
Hey, get back here, you!

216
00:11:50,442 --> 00:11:51,102
Hold on!

217
00:11:51,162 --> 00:11:52,862
What do you mean you're going to be a pirate?

218
00:11:53,082 --> 00:11:54,582
And stop ignoring me!

219
00:11:54,822 --> 00:11:55,242
Hey!

220
00:11:59,622 --> 00:12:01,962
He just got here, and he's already a pain.

221
00:12:02,222 --> 00:12:04,922
It's going to be like having a baby garp living with us.

222
00:12:05,002 --> 00:12:06,322
No, no, it's okay.

223
00:12:07,422 --> 00:12:07,902
Hey!

224
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:10,862
Wait for me!

225
00:12:10,862 --> 00:12:11,362
Hey!

226
00:12:12,802 --> 00:12:13,162
Hey!

227
00:12:16,882 --> 00:12:17,322
Hi!

228
00:12:17,462 --> 00:12:18,402
My name's Luffy!

229
00:12:18,782 --> 00:12:20,162
Everything's cool now!

230
00:12:20,282 --> 00:12:22,382
I'm not mad about you spitting on me!

231
00:12:22,382 --> 00:12:28,162
Why are you all laughing?

232
00:12:28,842 --> 00:12:30,842
But the guy just spilled some booze on me.

233
00:12:31,162 --> 00:12:32,822
It's not worth getting bent out of shape.

234
00:12:33,342 --> 00:12:35,202
It's not worth getting bent out of shape!

235
00:12:35,322 --> 00:12:36,642
I'd rather be friends!

236
00:12:37,422 --> 00:12:38,842
So can I come with you?

237
00:12:38,842 --> 00:13:02,122
Oh, my God!

238
00:13:02,122 --> 00:13:32,102
Oh, my God.

239
00:13:32,122 --> 00:14:02,102
Oh, my God.

240
00:14:02,122 --> 00:14:08,982
Ace is back.

241
00:14:09,202 --> 00:14:10,502
You know what that means.

242
00:14:10,942 --> 00:14:11,382
Boom!

243
00:14:14,002 --> 00:14:14,362
Huh?

244
00:14:14,662 --> 00:14:15,782
Wait, you're alone?

245
00:14:16,002 --> 00:14:16,962
That's not good.

246
00:14:17,582 --> 00:14:18,182
Oh, yeah.

247
00:14:18,502 --> 00:14:19,462
Where's Luffy?

248
00:14:19,882 --> 00:14:21,022
Wasn't he with you?

249
00:14:21,102 --> 00:14:21,662
Beats me.

250
00:14:21,662 --> 00:14:27,682
Come on, you snot-nosed brat.

251
00:14:28,022 --> 00:14:29,202
Where did you go?

252
00:14:29,602 --> 00:14:31,582
You think maybe he died out there?

253
00:14:32,142 --> 00:14:34,702
If he did, it's going to be our funeral, too.

254
00:14:35,002 --> 00:14:37,622
The boss must be worried sick right about now.

255
00:14:38,402 --> 00:14:38,722
Ugh.

256
00:14:39,382 --> 00:14:40,762
Get a hold of yourself.

257
00:14:41,002 --> 00:14:41,862
This is serious.

258
00:14:42,182 --> 00:14:43,022
No biggie.

259
00:14:43,282 --> 00:14:46,962
Oh, and is that what you're going to say to Garb when he finds out we let his grandson die?

260
00:14:47,022 --> 00:14:47,922
Why do you care?

261
00:14:48,222 --> 00:14:50,062
One less crappy brat in the world.

262
00:14:50,282 --> 00:14:52,862
I have a feeling that Garb won't see it that way.

263
00:14:52,862 --> 00:14:57,542
Well, maybe the old jackass should have thought about that before he left him with a bunch

264
00:14:57,542 --> 00:14:58,662
of bandits in the woods.

265
00:14:58,842 --> 00:15:01,082
Come on, does this look like a damn daycare to you?

266
00:15:01,322 --> 00:15:04,742
If he can't take care of the boy himself, he has no right to talk.

267
00:15:04,882 --> 00:15:06,702
You should tell him that, not us.

268
00:15:06,702 --> 00:15:07,462
Suck it!

269
00:15:21,802 --> 00:15:24,742
If Gold Roger had a son, what are you talking about?

270
00:15:25,602 --> 00:15:27,382
He'd end up just like his dad.

271
00:15:28,402 --> 00:15:29,902
Off with his damn head.

272
00:15:30,222 --> 00:15:33,122
Then he'd probably cry and shut him down for good.

273
00:15:33,982 --> 00:15:36,602
